Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 17:07:12 +0800
Subject: power: supply: piano_mca: apply Piano normal charging tables

Use the Piano CN normal CC/CV and JEITA tables with an 8 A
combined-cell ceiling, temperature recovery hysteresis and
profile-bound PMIC float voltage. Use the verified four-byte setter
for the normal 472 mA termination current.

Bind voltage and current updates to one ADSP and connector session.
HyperOS 4 returns successful empty FCC and ITERM readbacks, and the
model-0x56 FV getter uses twice the setter's step. Acknowledge the
original setters with their replies and session checks. Stop and
resume the PMIC through its charge-enable bit after fresh readings
and limit setup. Notify the gauge supply chain when measured net
current changes direction.

Confirm the pump stop before restoring the source policy. Keep the
bounded PMIC heat-sharing path, confirmed 3.5 s handover and factory
SC8541 protection. Pause PMIC charging during suspend and teardown,
when the host cannot enforce the JEITA policy.

Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia@gmail.com>
